<title>UK: Merrill Lynch increases Argentina-linked mark bond.</title>
<headline>Merrill Lynch increases Argentina-linked mark bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following repackaged bond, announced yesterday by lead manager Merrill Lynch (Deutschland), has been increased by 75 million marks bringing the total to 225 million marks. There are new issue and reoffer prices.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SIRES LINES ARGENTINA INVESTMENT BOND</p>
<p> AMT    225 MLN DEM   COUPON     13.0	MATURITY    07.APR.05</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.0     PAY DATE  S-22.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.50	REOFFER    99.0	S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> NOTES	AMORTISES IN SIX EQUAL ANNUAL INSTALLMENTS STARTING</p>
<p>		FROM 07.APR.00</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    FFT	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.0	 SELL CONC  1.50	LIST FEE    0.50</p>
<p> NOTES	CREDIT CALL PROVISIONS</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
